Renderer benchmark targets

GPU-facing benchmarks synchronize through Horse's backend-neutral Renderer::waitIdle() before recording wall time, so CPU command submission is not mistaken for completed GPU frame time. Median is the primary comparison; mean is printed as a noise indicator.

Forward+ lighting
  c run forward-plus-benchmark

  128 point + 128 spot lights at 1280x720.
  Compares the original full-light loop against Forward+ with alternating sample order.
  Use this result before adding depth slices.

Volumetrics
  c run volumetrics-benchmark

  Sweeps Low / Medium / High / Ultra at 1280x720.
  Compares Volumetrics disabled vs enabled for every quality level.
  Use this result before deciding whether froxel migration is justified.

Local shadows
  c run shadow-benchmark

  8 point + 8 spot shadow lights over 2048 triangles at Medium quality.
  Reports the cold dirty frame, steady cached frames, and one-light invalidation cost.
  Use this result before adding a dedicated local shadow atlas.

GI / BVH CPU
  c run gi-benchmark

  If Assets/Sponza/sponza.obj exists locally, it is used automatically.
  Otherwise the benchmark falls back to a deterministic 8192-triangle synthetic grid.
  Sweeps 1 / 4 / 8 triangles per BVH leaf and reports topology build, node count/depth, transform refit cost and probe traversal cost for each configuration.

  To measure another real GAME model:
    c build gi-benchmark
    ./build/debug/gi-benchmark "/absolute/path/to/model.gltf"

  Use representative real models before choosing the BVH leaf default or deciding whether TLAS/BLAS and baked/static probes are justified.
